  "_about": "Sentinel L4 golden set (PRD section 8.1, P4). Roughly 50 hand-labelled reports and 15 known duplicate clusters, replayed by scripts/evaluate.py on every deploy and compared against the recorded baseline (agents/av_sentinel/goldens/baseline.json).",
  "_format": "Same style as data/seed/m1_reports.json: hours_ago is relative to the run start, coordinates sit inside the fixture wards. expected_cluster is null for a report that must NOT merge with anything - a false merge on one of these is exactly what the false-merge-rate metric catches. expected_category is null only for the non-English fixtures, where nothing in this build could honestly produce one (see their notes).",
  "_language_note": "4 of the 50 reports are Kannada/Hindi, deliberately absent from data/seed/m1_reports.json because the lexical baseline (common/llm/heuristic.py) cannot classify them (PRD open question 3, ROADMAP Lane 3). They exercise the 'no ASR/vision provider, degrade honestly' path - recorded as unread with lowered confidence - not actual multilingual understanding. A real provider (Lane 4) is what would make expected_category answerable for these.",
